  "letSearch": {
    "_readme": "Gradient descent on u = log10(w) for the LET x dose penalty w (SquaredOverdosing on matRad's 'LETd' quantity, which is LET x dose). Outer objective J(w) = mean_s[ DxLETd_D2_s(w) / DxLETd_D2_s(dose-only) ] + lambda * P_cov(w), s = burdenStructures with a nonzero dose-only value. P_cov = sum of squared coverage violations in % (CTV D98 below minFractionOfRx*Rx; D98 more than maxD98DropPct below dose-only; D2 more than maxD2RisePct above dose-only). Central finite-difference gradient (step h decades), steepest-descent step eta*g capped at maxStepDecades, Armijo backtracking, move to a better finite-difference neighbour if there is one, bounds on w. Every LET plan starts from the dose-only spot weights, so J(w) is a deterministic function of w. Reference of the LET objective: refFactor x the 5th percentile of LET x dose (total, physical) in the CTV of the dose-only plan (Unkelbach 2016 style; CLAUDE.md 4.3). matRad divides it by numOfFractions like any dose level.",
    "w0": 0.1,
    "wMin": 0.001,
    "wMax": 3,
    "h": 0.15,
    "eta": 10.0,
    "maxStepDecades": 0.5,
    "tolStepDecades": 0.05,
    "armijoC": 0.0001,
    "maxBacktracks": 3,
    "maxEvals": 14,
    "lambda": 1.0,
    "refMode": "targetP5",
    "refFactor": 1.0,
    "letStructures": [
